 "Settings": "",
 "Stats, saves, skills, attacks, spells, inventory, feats, buffs and notes. The strip scrolls sideways, and you can swipe the page left or right to move between tabs.": "",
 "Stops the phone going to sleep while you play.": "",
 "Switch between Character, Party, Chat and Combat here. A number on Chat counts the messages you haven't seen.": "",
 "Switch between Character, Party, Chat, Combat and Map here. A number on Chat counts the messages you haven't seen.": "",
 "Tap an ability, save, skill, attack or spell to roll or use it at once. Press and hold for D35E's roll options first (a bonus, Take 10, optional feats). The ⓘ button shows an item's details.": "",
 "Tap to roll": "",
 "The character shown, and the scene it is on. Tap to switch characters if you have more than one. On a GM's phone, tap to choose any creature or NPC.": "",
 "The character's tabs": "",
 "The game's chat. Show all of it, or only rolls, damage and healing, or whispers.": "",
 "The Map view on or off, who sees your rolls (roll mode), and this tour.": "",
 "The password the mobile account logs in with. Players type it on their phone, so keep it simple.": "",
 "The player opens your game's address in the phone's browser and logs in as \"Name (Mobile)\" with that password. The phone's map is switched off for them (unless Map is ticked) and the VooDoo window fills the screen; its Settings has a tour of the window.\nMobile accounts show in the player list with a phone icon; the setting Hide mobile accounts in the player list leaves them out.": "",
 "The scene: tap a token to target it and place spell areas. Press and hold a token to open it; keep holding and drag your own token to move it.": "",
 "The turn order. Roll initiative, and end your turn when it is yours. On a GM's phone: start the combat, roll for NPCs and move the turns.": "",
 "Tick each player who needs a mobile account. Players who already have one show it instead of a box.": "",
 "Ticked, the phone gets a Map view to target tokens, move its own tokens and place spell areas by touch. Unticked, the phone has no map: lighter and faster. Players can switch it themselves in the phone's Settings.": "",
 "Type a message and send it. Chat commands work too: /roll 1d20, /w GM …": "",
